import json, re
from collections import Counter
from pathlib import Path
hexre = re.compile(r"\b[0-9a-f]{32,}\b")
keys = Counter()
for path in Path("claude-transcripts").rglob("*.jsonl"):
    for line in path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
        try: obj = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError: continue
        def walk(node, key=""):
            if isinstance(node, dict):
                for k, v in node.items(): walk(v, k)
            elif isinstance(node, list):
                for v in node: walk(v, key)
            elif isinstance(node, str) and hexre.search(node) and key in ("signature","id","uuid","requestId","sessionId","parentUuid","agentId","message_id","content","text","input"):
                keys[key] += 1
        walk(obj)
print(keys.most_common(10))
